`53 of 59 parts carry no property object` — the measurement that dominates this card.

## Done criterion 3 — `.epe` object count = base + planned additions

Cannot pass: there is no defensible planned-addition list until the weapon and light objects exist.
What was measured instead, on the graph every phase-B build inherits from test-091:

```
class                        vanilla  live  delta
CPartProp                           40     6    -34
totals 450 416
live .epe bytes 105430        # MODLOG §101/§102 recorded the repair as 109,526 -> 105,430 B
```

`450 − 416 = 34 = 40 − 6`, and the only class that differs is `CPartProp`: the §101 `.epe` repair
dropped 34 of the donor's 40 part props, and bm-001 → bm-002 → bm-009 have carried that loss since.
Fleet check (`E:\Modding\_JC3grab\detail`, 232 graphs): the `CPartProp` count equals the entity's
part count in **232/232** (cargo plane 161/161, fishing boat 103/103, …); the donor itself is the one
exception at 40/42.

## Exact blockers

1. **Step 2 (weapons) has prose, not values.** `t7_weapons_edits.json` `structural` = six
   `{"row","kind":"entity","what","note"}` rows (`"root main_weapon -> the cannon clone"`), no
   members. The tank's `CBulletWeaponBase w602_mediumtank_canon` / `w603_mediumtank_mgun` carry
   ~44 **unnamed (Jenkins-hashed)** members whose values matter; the detail caches keep only 6 named
   values per object, and the only extracted weapon graph in the tree is the APC's, whose unnamed
   members are w206-specific (`models/jc_weapons/04_mounted/w206_…`, `50CalBulletImpact`,
   `autoaim_assault_rifle`, `Fire` effect 1687852927). Cloning that template would ship an M2's
   effects on a 60 mm cannon — an R4 violation. B-06 (private `w6xx` copies) is later and `todo`.
2. **Step 3 (lights) needs 6 new `SVehicleLight` objects.** The graph holds 22 (16 + 6 lists); T-18's
   6 custom entries are `preset_id 0` objects whose 11 positional slots no file decodes (MODLOG
   §102d), so writing them is invention.
3. **Step 1 is a repair, not 19 inserts.** 32 of the 34 dropped props must come back (the two
   `door_f_*` ones name parts B-04 deleted) plus props for B-04's 19 new parts = 51 objects. All
   values are in hand (`_JC3grab/detail` + `Working/Parts/bm_vehicle_parts.json`), so this is the
   one step that is ready to build.
4. **Steps 4/5/6 are ready as written**: `t9_interaction.json` 85 objects / 84 transforms / 77
   placed / 6 hijack objects dropped; root `health` 100 `invulnerable` 0 stays per T-14 (36,000 is
   B-09's module); `CarCameraRef` + `bat_base.ctune` untouched.

